@startuml
title Deployment do nnet-agent

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

node "Host A (baremetal)" {
    component "nnetd\n(controller)" as NNETDA
    component "br-prod\n10.100.0.1/24\ntags: [it, external]" as BRA
    component "vxlan-prod\nVNI 100" as VXA

    NNETDA -down-> BRA : publica\n239.8.0.100:4790\nTTL=1
    BRA -down- VXA

    node "VM a1" {
        component "nnet-agent" as AGA
        component "ens3\n10.100.0.50/24" as NICA
        AGA -down-> NICA : aplica IP fixo\ne rotas (proto 98)
    }
    BRA -down- NICA
}

node "Host B (baremetal)" {
    component "nnetd\n(controller)" as NNETDB
    component "br-prod\n10.100.0.2/24\ntags: [it, external]" as BRB
    component "vxlan-prod\nVNI 100" as VXB

    NNETDB -down-> BRB : publica\n239.8.0.100:4790
    BRB -down- VXB

    node "VM b1" {
        component "nnet-agent" as AGB
        component "ens3\n10.100.0.51/24" as NICB
        AGB -down-> NICB
    }
    BRB -down- NICB
}

VXA -right- VXB : underlay UDP 4789

note bottom
  O segmento L2 atravessa os dois hosts pelo VXLAN, então o anúncio
  multicast do host A também chega à VM b1. Por isso o agente mantém
  estado por controller_id, com lease independente: quando o nnetd do
  host A para, apenas as rotas dele expiram.
end note

@enduml
